## Exact factorization

Write the selected H02 complement chart as

```text
A(a,gamma) = A0(gamma) + a Delta_C(gamma),
```

where `A0` is the B89 chart and `Delta_C` is the G3BI correction. The G3BZ
rank witness selects `6,022` rows and `6,022` columns. From the six exact
`Z[gamma]` coefficient matrices define

```text
U = Delta_C[:, selected columns],
W = Delta_C[selected rows, :],
S = Delta_C[selected rows, selected columns].
```

The selected specialization has nonzero minor determinant `10028 mod 21817`,
so `S` is invertible over `Q(gamma)`. Since G3BZ independently proves
`rank(Delta_C)=6022`, exact linear algebra gives

```text
Delta_C = U S^-1 W,
```

equivalently

```text
Delta_C det(S) = U adj(S) W.
```

All eighteen polynomial submatrices are emitted. At the selected split place,
the independent block replay reconstructs every component of `Delta_C` with
zero mismatch; the component ranks sum to `6,022`.

## Reduced inverse equation

For

```text
P  = A0^-1 U,
x0 = A0^-1 b,
```

the full `42,458`-dimensional equation is exactly equivalent to

```text
(S + a W P) z = a W x0,
x = x0 - P z.
```

Thus the selected H02 varying solve has dimension `6,022`, not `42,458`.
This is an exact rank factorization, not a low-rank approximation.

